course: dictionary
lesson: 14219
title: Mustang: a horse or a car?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mustang is a small, tough horse that lives half-wild in the western United States. «The mustang galloped across the dry plain, its mane flying in the wind.» The clues are galloped, dry plain and flying mane, so you can picture a horse running free.
explain: Mustangs are feral, which means their ancestors were tame, but they now live wild. «Long ago, horses brought by the Spanish became the ancestors of the mustangs.» So a mustang is a horse, but not a pet: it has a wild life.
explain: Look at the capital M in «Dad drove the shiny red Mustang to the shop.» A capital letter often means a name. The Mustang here is a famous car, not a horse. Check the words around it: a car, a shop and a drive tell you which meaning is right.
fact: Mustang is a noun: a mustang, mustangs.
fact: «Mustang» means a small, tough, half-wild horse of the western USA.
fact: Mustangs are feral: their ancestors were tame horses, brought by the Spanish, but they live wild.
fact: With a capital M, «Mustang» is a name, such as the Ford Mustang car or the P-51 Mustang plane.
fact: Use the clues around the word, like «galloped» or «drove», to tell which meaning the writer means.
exercise: «The mustang galloped across the dry plain, its mane flying in the wind.» What is a mustang? | *A small, tough, half-wild horse | A tall tree that grows in the desert | A large, slow cow from the farm | A type of cowboy hat
exercise: «Dad drove the shiny red Mustang to the shop.» What does the capital M tell you? | It means a horse | *It is a name, like the Ford Mustang car | It means a grey, wet day | It means very fast
exercise: Mustangs now live wild, but long ago their families were tame. What does this tell you about mustangs? | They live in the sea | They were always wild, never tame | They are tame pets in a house | *Their ancestors were tame horses, but they now live wild
test: Which word means a small, tough, half-wild horse of the western USA? | Donkey | *Mustang | Pony | Camel
test: «Tom read about the Mustang fighter plane in his history book.» What does the capital M show? | A horse | A very old word | *A name | A sad feeling
exam: «The mustang ran free across the American West.» What is a mustang? | A car that goes very fast | *A small, tough, half-wild horse of the western USA | A wild horse from the western USA | A tame pet dog that lives in a house
